<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yonezawa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yonezawa is a city in the south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamagata-prefecture">Yamagata Prefecture</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. The Date clan made it their seat in 1548, and from 1601 it was the castle town of the Uesugi clan, whose lord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uesugi-harunori">Uesugi Harunori</a> (Yōzan) reformed the domain's finances in the 18th century. The city is known for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> weaving and for Yonezawa beef.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yonezawa.jpg" alt="Yonezawa" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Kano assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:YonezawaCityMountainView.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
